CALL newPutForth(230, 1, 'Climate change is a hoax perpetuated by academics chasing grant money, politicians chasing control, and corporations chasing subsidies. Real science doesn\'t silence debate — climate science does.');
CALL newPutForth(415, 1, 'Wind and solar go dark when the wind stops blowing and the sun goes down. Ask Texas in February 2021. Reliable baseload power isn\'t optional — it\'s what a modern economy is built on.');
CALL newPutForth(478, 1, 'Want clean, reliable, zero-carbon power? Nuclear. France gets 70% of its electricity from nuclear. Zero emissions. If climate change were the real emergency Democrats claim, they\'d embrace it. They don\'t.');
CALL newPutForth(479, 1, 'Chernobyl killed 31 people directly. Coal kills 800,000 a year from air pollution. Nuclear\'s safety record is the best of any energy source per kilowatt-hour produced. That\'s not opinion — that\'s the data.');
CALL newPutForth(480, 1, 'Nuclear plants emit near-zero greenhouse gases during operation and run 24/7 regardless of weather. Cleanest, most reliable power source we have. Should be the obvious choice for anyone serious about emissions.');
CALL newPutForth(527, 1, 'Green New Deal would cost $93 trillion by progressive economists\' own estimates. We\'d destroy U.S. manufacturing, farming, and energy before we moved the global temperature needle one degree.');
CALL newPutForth(528, 1, 'We don\'t have batteries that can store a week\'s worth of grid power. We don\'t have solar that works in a Minnesota winter. We\'re not close to ready to bet the entire economy on wind and sun.');
CALL newPutForth(529, 1, 'Humanity survived the Medieval Warm Period, the Little Ice Age, the Black Death, two World Wars, and dozens of catastrophes. We adapt. That\'s what humans do better than any other species.');
CALL newPutForth(530, 1, 'Open the regulatory pathway for advanced nuclear, geothermal, carbon capture. Stop blocking innovation with permitting delays that stretch to decades. Technology solves problems — mandates just raise costs.');
CALL newPutForth(730, 1, 'Advanced nuclear, carbon capture, precision fermentation — new technology will do more to cut emissions than any government mandate. Set the goal, let engineers figure out the path. That\'s how innovation works.');
CALL newPutForth(865, 1, 'Eliminating fossil fuels by 2035 — as progressives demand — would wipe out 8 million direct energy jobs, send utility bills through the roof, and crush the manufacturing base we haven\'t even started to rebuild.');
CALL newPutForth(868, 1, 'Collective action only works when people believe the sacrifice is shared equally. When climate activists fly private jets and live in mansions, they\'re telling everyone else the rules don\'t apply to them.');
CALL newPutForth(869, 1, 'Effective collective action requires that people trust the institutions asking them to sacrifice. Most Americans distrust government and the climate establishment right now. You don\'t get to skip that step.');
CALL newPutForth(870, 1, 'Business exists to generate returns — that\'s not a criticism, that\'s the feature. It\'s why markets are efficient. Forcing businesses to prioritize collective climate goals fights the basic incentive structure.');
CALL newPutForth(1010, 1, 'China\'s one-child policy sterilized millions of women, mostly by force, mostly in rural areas. Population control has never been done equitably. It always falls on those with the least power to resist.');
CALL newPutForth(1011, 1, 'Energy efficiency is a real goal — lower costs for consumers and businesses, better engineering, less waste. That\'s good economics regardless of what you believe about climate. The mandate isn\'t needed.');
CALL newPutForth(1034, 1, 'U.S. nuclear plants spend more on regulatory compliance than on operations. NRC permitting has driven construction costs to $30 billion per reactor. We regulated ourselves out of the cleanest energy source we had.');
CALL newPutForth(1035, 1, 'Recycling felt good, so we did it. China stopped taking U.S. recyclables in 2018 and most of it went straight to landfill anyway. It was always more about feeling virtuous than actually helping the environment.');
CALL newPutForth(1036, 1, 'Reducing waste at the source — making less of it in the first place — beats sorting through contaminated mixed streams after the fact. Recycling manages the symptom. Source reduction treats the disease.');
CALL newPutForth(1037, 1, 'Most cities lose money on recycling programs. Sorted materials are often too contaminated to process. The trucks burn diesel. The sorting facilities cost millions. The economics have never worked.');
CALL newPutForth(1038, 1, 'Accepting glass, wet cardboard, and mixed plastics together guarantees contamination that renders the whole batch landfill-bound anyway. The programs are structured to fail from the start.');
CALL newPutForth(1039, 1, 'Modern engineered landfills have geomembrane liners, leachate collection, and methane capture systems. They\'re carefully monitored. They\'re not the open dumps from 1965. Time to update the narrative.');
CALL newPutForth(1040, 1, 'Landfills get blamed based on poorly run facilities from 50 years ago. A modern engineered landfill is a completely different structure — managed, monitored, and better than most people think.');
CALL newPutForth(1041, 1, 'Waste-to-energy incineration cuts volume by 90%, recovers ferrous metals, and generates electricity. Stockholm heats 250,000 homes this way. We built a few in the 1970s and then froze our thinking.');
CALL newPutForth(1042, 1, 'Incineration with energy recovery beats landfill on greenhouse gases, land use, and methane. Landfill methane is 25x more potent than CO2. Waste-to-energy is the pragmatic answer we keep ignoring.');
CALL newPutForth(1043, 1, 'Incinerators use magnetic separation to recover nearly all ferrous metal — the highest-value recyclable — before combustion. You get energy production AND metals recovery. Best of both approaches.');
CALL newPutForth(1044, 1, 'Paper, cardboard, food waste, wood — plant-based materials are the majority of what goes into a municipal incinerator. Plant-based carbon is part of the natural cycle. Completely different math from fossil fuels.');
